    <span class="section-kicker">IMSA</span>
    <h2>Indian Mathematics and Science Association</h2>
    <p>The Indian Mathematics and Science Association (IMSA) was established in 2018 and is registered under the Societies Registration Act, 1860 (Registration No. S000234, 2025–26).</p>
    <p>The IMSA is committed to advancing mathematics and science through research and scholarly publications. It publishes the International Journal of the Indian Mathematics and Science Association (IJIMSA), covering Mathematical Sciences, Biological Sciences, and Chemical Sciences.</p>
    <p>The Association also organizes the Aryabhatta Talent Search Tests for students of Classes VI–XII and Undergraduate (UG) and Postgraduate (PG) levels. Under its IMSA Olympiad Ecosystem, outstanding students are recognized with laptops, cash prizes, medals, certificates, and training programmes.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="org-card"><img src="Images/image1.jpeg" alt="IMSA logo" /><h3>Indian Mathematics &amp; Science Association</h3><p>Research · Scholarly publications · Talent search · Olympiad ecosystem</p></div>
</div></section>
